  "final": "`DocumentService.archive` in `src/service.ts` now enforces the authorization rules. `tsc -p tsconfig.json && node checks/public.cjs` passes, including the new checks I added.\n\nThe method works in this order:\n1. **Visibility:** it throws `Error('not found')` if the document is missing, deleted, or in another tenant. This applies to admins too.\n2. **Permission:** an admin may archive any visible document. An editor may archive only a document they own. A viewer, or any other role value, gets `Error('forbidden')`.\n3. **Archive:** if the document isn't archived yet, it calls the repository's `archive`, which sets `archived` to true and appends `{actor: actor.user, document: id}` to the audit. If it's already archived, nothing happens.\n\nPermission is checked before the already-archived no-op, so an unauthorized actor still gets `forbidden` on an archived document. Both errors are thrown before anything is written, so a failed call leaves documents and audit unchanged.\n\nI appended checks to `checks/public.cjs`. They cover missing, deleted and foreign-tenant documents (`not found`), a viewer and a non-owner editor (`forbidden`), and no change to documents or audit after those failures. They also cover an owner editor archiving successfully with a single audit entry, and a repeat archive adding no second entry. I didn't test an unrecognized role value; the code rejects it as `forbidden`.\n\nI didn't change any public interfaces.",
